-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",21,{
[641]="7004E494\n1\tDestroy grappling hooks at Skald's Drop (total: 8)\tGrappling hooks can be found along the edge of Skald's Drop in the Ironfold. After discovering that the Jangovar have been attempting to scale Skald's Drop, Slegi has asked you to destroy any grappling hooks you find.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have destroyed many of the grappling hooks used by the Jangovar at Skald's Drop.\n",
[642]="700450F0\n1\tTalk to the shepherd\tThe shepherd and Lady Glánhar stand at the centre of Ost Rimmon. Lady Glánhar cannot make out what the flustered shepherd is trying to tell her. You should speak to him yourself and see if you can get anything out of him.\n2\tTalk to Lady Glánhar\tThe shepherd and Lady Glánhar stand at the centre of Ost Rimmon. You should tell the shepherd's message to Lady Glánhar: that she is to meet the captor on the eastern slope of Calenhad to bargain for the lives of her three sons.\n3\tFind Gondrad\tLady Glánhar asked you to find Gondrad, who should be found somewhere within Ost Rimmon.\n4\tTalk to Lady Glánhar\tLady Glánhar stands at the centre of Ost Rimmon. You should go with Gondrad and learn what Lady Glánhar wishes to do about the ransomer.\n5\tMeet the ransomer\tGo to the meeting-spot, south-east of Calenhad, on the bank above the river Sírnarthan.\n6\tDefeat the ambushers\tAmbushers have jumped out of concealment on the way to meeting the ransomer. Defend yourself!\n7\tGo on to meet the ransomer\tContinue looking for the meeting-spot, south-east of Calenhad, on the bank above the river.\n8\tTalk to the Variag Captain\tThe the meeting-spot is south-east of Calenhad, on the bank above the river. Talk to the Variag Captain and learn what he wants for the lives of Glánhar's sons.\n9\tReturn to Glánhar\tLady Glánhar stand at the centre of Ost Rimmon. You should return to Lady Glánhar with the Jarl Akhiz's demands.\n",
[643]="7007177A\n1\tTalk to Faeron\tYou should talk to Faeron at Gadim-ûn to ask if he will accompany you.\n2\tComplete Instance: A Personal Matter\tNabatínu has asked you for the personal favour of checking on the welfare of his wife, Kugâna, a Jatsakóri still under the thrall of the Bokhóri sorceresses. You should talk to Faeron at Gadim-ûn when you are ready to go, and the Ranger will accompany you.\n3\tTalk to Nabatínu\tIn the company of Faeron, you travelled to Gebarakór, where you witnessed the arrival of Ombátha, the leader of the Bokhóri. You also spotted Nabatínu's wife, Kugâna, who was alive but did not look well.\n",
[644]="7006EC05\n1\tFree prisoners (total: 8)\030Defeat Ekhamâti look-outs (total: 6)\tYour mission is to reach the Ekhamâti camp where they are holding prisoners and free any that you can. Then put an end to the executioner before he can harm any more people.\n2\tDefeat Ekhamâti executioner\tFind and defeat the Ekhamâti executioner!\n",
[645]="70025A46\n1\tFind a Ranger at the colossus-camp to speak with about the weeds you found\tThe colossus-camp is north of the Barandalf. One of the Rangers at the colossus-camp may be interested in seeing the weeds you have found.\n",
[646]="70009F57\n1\tTalk to Calenglad\tCalenglad is at the Ranger-camp on the island of Tinnudir, off the east shore of Lake Nenuial, west of Parth Aduial in Evendim. Evendim is west of the North Downs and north of the Shire. The Ranger Ferrif has asked you to speak with his leader Calenglad in his stead.\n",
[647]="700372E0\n1\tDefend the supplies and store-houses from waves of enemies ([see journal]/7)\tThe equipment store-houses and stockpiles of supplies must be secured before the invading army can destroy them. Schematics can be picked up and stored at the water-mill. The larger provisions must be defended from direct attacks. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[648]="7003E5B8\n1\tComplete \"The Riddle-game\" quest arc\030Complete \"Frodo's Burden\"\tBilbo Baggins is in the Hall of Fire on the north side of the ground floor in the Last Homely House. Gandalf the Grey is in Bilbo's apartments on the south side. Elrond bade you take some rest while in Rivendell and to speak with two of his guests: Bilbo Baggins and Gandalf the Grey.\n2\tTalk to Elrond\tMaster Elrond is in his library on the top floor of the Last Homely House. You should return to Elrond and let him know that you have done as he had suggested.\n",
[649]="70007B41\n1\tBurn bloated corpses (quantity: see journal)\030Burn barrels of rotting flesh (quantity: see journal)\tThe source of the plague can be found in the encampments of the Orcs at Ost Cyrn, south of Ost Guruth. The Orcs care little about the disease spreading from the corpses and barrels of viscera littering their camp. Stanric gave you his tinderbox and bid you burn out the disease spreading from Ost Cyrn.\n2\tReturn tinderbox to Stanric at Ost Guruth\tStanric awaits the return of his tinderbox at Ost Guruth, north of Ost Cyrn. You set fire to the corpses and barrels at the Orc-camp in an effort to avoid the spread of plague. You should return to Stanric with word of your success.\n",
[650]="7003EAF9\n1\tDefeat cave-claws in the North Trollshaws (total: 6)\tCave-claws can be found in the North Trollshaws, in the gorges south of Thoroniel's encampment. Thoroniel has asked you and your companions to hunt the foul cave-claws of the North Trollshaws.\n2\tTalk to Thoroniel\tThoroniel is posted north of the cave-claw infested gorges in the North Trollshaws. You should return to Thoroniel and let her know that you have done as she has asked.\n",
[651]="7003EBE5\n1\tDefeat sickle-flies in the South Trollshaws (total: 6)\tThere are sickle-flies in the South Trollshaws. While in the South Trollshaws, you should purge the infestation of sickle-flies.\n",
[652]="70015E49\n1\tDefeat lizards (total: 14)\tLizards can be found in Ulundín in the southern tip of Emyn Naer, south-west of Echad Dúnann. Tinúriel has asked that you slay the lizards who have been killing off the native creatures of Eregion.\n2\tTalk to Tinúriel at Echad Dúnann\tTinúriel is at Echad Dúnann, north-east of Ulundín. You should return to Tinúriel and inform her that you have slain many lizards.\n",
[653]="7006BF3B\n1\tDefeat Ordâkhai at Ghât Lor (total: 15)\tDestroy fortifications and defeat Ordâkhai at Ghât Lor. Ghât Lor can be found east of Vartúlin.\n2\tReturn to Artar Ildarthos at Vartúlin with news of your triumph\tReturn to Artar Ildarthos at Vartúlin with news of your triumph.\n",
[654]="70007B90\n1\tDefeat spiders in Amon Ros (total: 10)\tSpiders dwell in the shade of Amon Ros, west of Ost Guruth. With undeniable hatred towards spiders, Tortwil asked you to enter the ruins of Amon Ros to strike at the vile creatures dwelling there.\n2\tTalk to Tortwil\tTortwil awaits your return at Ost Guruth, east of Amon Ros. You should return to Tortwil and tell him of the destruction wrought upon the spiders. He should be pleased with your success.\n",
[655]="70041362\n1\tThe hamlet of Tungobel can be found north-east of Erchar's encampment. Rescue the townsfolk from the Corsair and Haradrim forces.\t\n2\tSpeak with Erchar and inform him of your success\tErchar can be found at his encampment in the western end of Dor-en-Ernil, south-west of Tungobel. You should speak with Erchar.\n",
[656]="70015E11\n1\tDefeat the messenger\tThe Messenger is west of Porth Cadlus, south-west of Echad Dúnann and across Nan Sirannon. You must stop the Dunlanding Messenger from receiving reinforcements from Nan Sirannon.\n2\tTalk to Glavroleth at Echad Dúnann\tGlavroleth is north-east of Porth Cadlus in Echad Dúnann. You should return to Glavroleth and inform her of your success.\n",
[657]="70041478\n1\tSearch for the mere on the Gilrain\tThe mere can be found far to the north and slightly east of Linhir in Dor-en-Ernil. Tancestel has asked you to bring his river-stone to the great mere along the Gilrain.\n2\tPlace Tancestel's river-stone on a pile of stones\tThe pile of river-stones can be found at the edge of the mere along the Gilrain. You have arrived at the mere on the Gilrain and should now place Tancestel's river-stone.\n3\tKneel before the mysterious woman\tThe mysterious woman can be found on the banks of the mere. You have placed the stone, and now a mysterious woman has appeared. If what Tancestel said is true, you should honour her by kneeling before her.\n4\tTalk to the mysterious woman\tThe mysterious woman can be found on the banks of the mere. You have honoured the mysterious woman and should now attempt to speak with her.\n5\tFollow the woman into the mere\tThe centre of the mere can be found in north-eastern Dor-en-Ernil. The mysterious woman has begun to walk into the centre of the mere. You should follow her.\n6\tTalk to Roamingstar, Maiden of Gilrain\tRoamingstar can be found in her glade in north-eastern Dor-en-Ernil. You have been ferried to a beautiful glade by the mysterious woman, and should now speak to her.\n",
[658]="70009EF9\n1\tTalk to Sergeant-at-Arms Ascwyn\tSergeant-at-Arms Ascwyn is at Glân Vraig in the Ettenmoors. Captain-General Lainedhel's emissaries are asking any would-be heroes to make their way into the Ettenmoors to bolster their small numbers. Many stable-masters have trained horses who can take you to the Ettenmoors. You should speak with Sergeant-at-Arms Ascwyn upon your arrival there.\n",
[659]="70022D5E\n1\tTrestlebridge can be found north of Bree along the Greenway. Make your way there and speak with the folk who make the beleaguered town their home. The letter requested that you make your way to Trestlebridge to talk to the people there.\t\n",
[660]="700301D9\n1\tTry to beg Baillas awake\tBaillas is near the centre of Fangorn's eaves. You should beg Baillas to wake him up and enlist his help in finding a man who may be in grave peril. You must select the intended target and perform an emote to advance this quest.\n2\tBecome angry at Baillas to rouse him\tBaillas is near the centre of Fangorn's eaves. You should become angry at Baillas to wake him up and enlist his help in finding a man who may be in grave peril. You must select the intended target and perform an emote to advance this quest.\n3\tFind Léofmar\tLéofmar is somewhere in Fangorn, probably not far from his original camp-site. You should search to the north-west of the site. You should find Léofmar before it is too late.\n",
[661]="70020F00\n1\tDefeat Lhew\tLhew is at Lhe Lhechu, south-west of Echad Dagoras. Dagoras has asked you to defeat Lhew, commander of the band of Dunlending deserters in Fordirith.\n2\tTalk to Dagoras at Echad Dagoras\tDagoras is at Echad Dagoras, north-east of Lhe Lhechu. You should speak with Dagoras and let him know that Lhew has been defeated.\n",
[662]="7001AD29\n1\tDefeat Orc-scouts in Taur Morvith (total: 6)\030Collect Gathbúrz message\tOrc-scouts can be found throughout Taur Morvith. Iavassúl asked you to defeat the Orc-scouts ranging outside of the forts in Taur Morvith and to intercept any messages they might be trying to carry through to Gathbúrz.\n2\tTalk to Iavassúl at Iavassúl's Watch\tIavassúl is at Iavassúl's Watch in Taur Morvith. You should bring the message you intercepted to Iavassúl.\n",
[663]="7001BE58\n1\tFind and return the pendant to its owner\tThe pendant is far too well-crafted to belong to a goblin. You should ask folk at The Forsaken Inn or the Ranger Candaith at his camp in the western shadow of Weathertop if they know to whom the pendant may belong.\n",
[664]="70002C6D\n1\tOrc encampments can be found to the north-east of Trestlebridge. You should search Orc encampments for signs that the guards of Trestlebridge were drugged before the attack, proving Talbot's innocence.\t\n2\tBring the sleeping draught to Talbot Hinton\tTalbot Hinton can be found in Trestlebridge. At the Orc camps north of Trestlebridge, you were able to find cauldrons of a vile liquid, and collect some of the contents.\n",
[665]="7002D52D\n1\tTalk to the Bree Postmaster\tSpeak to the Bree Postmaster to request a Postman's Badge, in order to assist with finding the lost invitations.\n",
[666]="70002D15\n1\tCollect red lovage (total: 4)\030Collect silverbell (total: 3)\030Collect spiky mugwort (total: 3)\tSpiky mugwort, silverbell, and red lovage can be found in the lands around Fail-á-Khro and the northern city of Donnvail: spiky mugwort near the ponds south-west of Fail-á-Khro; red lovage by the farms outside Donnvail; and silverbell by the fortress of Tór Gailvin, to the east. Cána has asked you to gather some herbs so she can make a poultice to heal the hurts of those injured in the battles sure to come.\n2\tBring the herbs to Cána\tCána is at Fail-á-Khro, north of Aughaire along the road. Cána has asked you to bring her the herbs she needs to make a healing poultice for her people.\n",
[667]="7006852D\n1\tDefeat Corsairs in the Gut (total: 6)\030Fake sashes planted (total: 6)\tHadorion seeks to sow chaos amongst Khâshap's rivals by framing him for acts of aggression.\n2\tTalk to Hadorion\tYou should tell Hadorion that you have created some chaos in the Gut and the fake sashes have been planted. Hadorion can be found in the Lower Ward.\n",
[668]="7002BFB3\n1\tCollect avanc-hides (total: 8)\tAvanc can be found throughout the Rushgore. Amal has asked you to hunt avanc for their hides.\n2\tBring the avanc-hides to Amal at the Woodman camp in the Rushgore\tAmal is at the Woodman camp at the heart of the Rushgore. You should bring the avanc-hides you collected to Amal.\n",
[669]="70022D45\n1\tBring the note to Albra Lowbanks in Bree\tAlbra Lowbanks sent you a letter requesting that you visit her in the training hall in Bree. Deliver the letter to Albra. She can be found in the training hall for burglars beneath the Mud-gate.\n",
[670]="70022D60\n1\tBring the letter to Burt Nine-tales\tBurt Nine-tales sent you a letter requesting that you visit him at the Prancing Pony in Bree. Deliver the letter to Burt Nine-tales at the Prancing Pony in Bree.\n",
[671]="70022D61\n1\tBring the letter to Dawn Appledore in Bree\tDawn Appledore sent you a letter requesting that you visit her in the Bree Jail. Deliver the letter to Dawn Appledore. She can be found in the Bree Jail.\n",
[672]="70022D65\n1\tBring the letter to Dalton Willow in Bree\tDalton Willow sent you a letter requesting that you visit him in Bree. Deliver the letter to Dalton Willow. He can be found at the Scholar's Stair in Bree.\n",
})
